SENTINEL-1

Radar features were derived from COPERNICUS/S1_GRD in Google Earth Engine and
remain subject to the Copernicus Sentinel Data Terms and Conditions. Cite the
Copernicus Sentinel programme and the source product when reusing them.

NASA SMAP

Soil-moisture comparison features were derived from
NASA/SMAP/SPL4SMGP/007. NASA states that this dataset is in the public domain
and available without restriction on use and distribution. Version 7 has been
superseded by version 8; it is retained here solely to reproduce the historical
experiment. Recommended product citation:

  Reichle, R. H. et al. (2022). SMAP L4 Global 3-hourly 9 km EASE-Grid
  Surface and Root Zone Soil Moisture Analysis Update, Version 7. NASA NSIDC
  DAAC. https://doi.org/10.5067/LWJ6TF5SZRG3

COPERNICUS GLOBAL LAND COVER

The habitat masks were derived from Copernicus Global Land Cover products and
remain subject to the source product's terms. The Somaliland mask uses a
documented reconstruction described in somaliland_test/README.md.
